Description: common: bail out when escaped labels can't fit into ret
 Fixes an out-of-bounds read (and a truncated/garbage normalized name) when
 avahi_escape_label() fails because the escaped label does not fit into the
 remaining buffer: avahi_normalize_name() ignored the failure, returned a
 non-NULL but unterminated buffer, and avahi_normalize_name_strdup() then ran
 strlen() past it.  This is a follow-up to 94cb648 ("Ensure each label is at
 least one byte long") and makes the CVE-2026-59987 guard effective for names
 whose escaped form overflows while still ending on a label boundary.
Author: Evgeny Vereshchagin <evvers@ya.ru>
Origin: https://github.com/avahi/avahi/commit/20dec84b2480821704258bc908e7b2bd2e883b24
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
---
diff --git a/avahi-common/domain.c b/avahi-common/domain.c
index 3b1ab68..f547453 100644
--- a/avahi-common/domain.c
+++ b/avahi-common/domain.c
@@ -210,7 +210,8 @@ char *avahi_normalize_name(const char *s, char *ret_s, size_t size) {
         } else
             empty = 0;
 
-        avahi_escape_label(label, strlen(label), &r, &size);
+        if (!(avahi_escape_label(label, strlen(label), &r, &size)))
+            return NULL;
     }
 
     return ret_s;
